{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T13:34:01.715399Z","id":"f86aa2227457ef0937c3a2d4740bb9beb5495ff8909c090f365451f089270601","body":{"detail":"Not taken for now: it needs a pinned nightly toolchain and either a third-party extractor (building Charon from source is an unreviewed external build) or Provium's own reimplementation of control-flow reconstruction from the MIR graph, and its output is further from the source (iterators as next() loops, basic blocks), which makes consumer proofs harder to read. The syn front end plus Lean's elaborator re-checking every generated definition, and differential scenarios, are used instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"988af2d0fe33103dc597afef789c33e1b6afaa274865f0bb2d14a658ab7ccd32"},"summary":"Compiler MIR (Charon LLBC or a rustc_public driver) as the typed backend's front end","tags":["revisit:closing the front-end trust gap for CORRECTNESS_PLAN P10/M6, or a construct whose types syn-level inference cannot determine","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T13:34:01.715662Z","id":"1d9b6ee5113f5e506c7da76e82a82113b09c22706b4602e4cd4dbb3c188a3569","body":{"detail":"Replacing Rust.saturating_sub with a wrong definition still passes jarl/proofs/engine (40 seeds x 400 steps): the scenario never executes it. Paths needing joint membership hooks (AppendBatch, quorum checks), snapshot installation from a leader, and Full rejections are also unreached by a fixed three-node cluster with only Node's public API.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"2d999780867b1e413836172b9ba2ea926e47f6dcb235247d01cd7108311d9dd2"},"suggested_fix":"Report per-function coverage of the Lean evaluation (count calls per generated definition) and fail when a root's reachable definitions are never executed; extend the scenario with a lagging follower to force Install and Full paths.","summary":"Jarl's differential scenario does not reach every translated operation","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T16:18:14.989404Z","id":"89d297ebf4dc53c5c592f649b6ded9fdf2b3c3c34a16549c4a86766ce314c918","body":{"detail":"Replacing Rust.saturating_sub with a wrong definition still passes jarl/proofs/engine (40 seeds x 400 steps): the scenario never executes it. Paths needing joint membership hooks (AppendBatch, quorum checks), snapshot installation from a leader, and Full rejections are also unreached by a fixed three-node cluster with only Node's public API.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"2d999780867b1e413836172b9ba2ea926e47f6dcb235247d01cd7108311d9dd2"},"suggested_fix":"Report per-function coverage of the Lean evaluation (count calls per generated definition) and fail when a root's reachable definitions are never executed; extend the scenario with a lagging follower to force Install and Full paths.","summary":"Jarl's differential scenario does not reach every translated operation","supersedes":"1d9b6ee5113f5e506c7da76e82a82113b09c22706b4602e4cd4dbb3c188a3569","tags":["session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-04T16:18:14.989598Z","id":"6ba04106ad848c3c8cef14daf6cefd02c6bed32857a5831786141e4850ffb677","body":{"detail":"Not taken for now: it needs a pinned nightly toolchain and either a third-party extractor (building Charon from source is an unreviewed external build) or Provium's own reimplementation of control-flow reconstruction from the MIR graph, and its output is further from the source (iterators as next() loops, basic blocks), which makes consumer proofs harder to read. The syn front end plus Lean's elaborator re-checking every generated definition, and differential scenarios, are used instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"988af2d0fe33103dc597afef789c33e1b6afaa274865f0bb2d14a658ab7ccd32"},"summary":"Compiler MIR (Charon LLBC or a rustc_public driver) as the typed backend's front end","supersedes":"f86aa2227457ef0937c3a2d4740bb9beb5495ff8909c090f365451f089270601","tags":["revisit:closing the front-end trust gap for CORRECTNESS_PLAN P10/M6, or a construct whose types syn-level inference cannot determine","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
